*Data of Table 1:*

$1^{\mathrm{st}}$ column is the number of the nova;

$2^{\mathrm{nd}}$ – the time of the maximum brightness of the nova, $T_0$, in Julian Days (JD);

$3^{\mathrm{rd}}$ – the apparent magnitude of the nova at maximum brightness, $m_{V\mathrm{max}}$;

$4^{\mathrm{th}}$ – the rate of decline, i.e. the time that it takes the nova to drop by 2 magnitudes below maximum, $t_2$, in days (d);

$5^{\mathrm{th}}$ – the angular radius of the expanding shell of the nova, $\theta$ (in arcsec);

$6^{\mathrm{th}}$ – the time of the measurement of the radius of the nova shell, $T$, in Julian Days (JD);

$7^{\mathrm{th}}$ – the rate of expansion of the shell of the nova, $v$, in km/s;

$8^{\mathrm{th}}$ – the interstellar extinction in the direction of the nova, $A_\mathrm{V}$.

*Data of Table 2:*

$1^{\mathrm{st}}$ column is the time of observation in Julian Days (JD);

$2^{\mathrm{nd}}$ – the apparent magnitude of the nova.

